## Testing

**TDD:** write a failing test first for new functions, API endpoints, business logic, and bug fixes (reproduce first). Confirm it fails because the feature is missing, not from a syntax error. Skip for docs, config, dependency versions, and formatting.

- Naming: Python `test_<func>_<scenario>_<expected>` | TS `it("should <behavior> when <condition>")`
- Markers: `@pytest.mark.unit` (mock all I/O, < 1ms) | `@pytest.mark.integration` (real test deps, fixtures, cleanup)
- Mock where imported, not where defined. A unit test > 1s likely has unmocked I/O.
- Minimum 80% coverage on changed lines (CI-enforced per PR; check locally with `make diff-coverage`). Run the full suite, not just files you touched.
